# Repo-root .easignore -- EAS Build archives from the git repository root by
# default (monorepo support), not just phc-local-app/mobile/ where app.json
# actually lives. Without this, it was trying to compress the whole ~8GB
# monorepo (central-system/backend/ml-pipeline alone is ~8GB, .git is
# 3.6GB) -- the real cause of a build that hung at "Compressing project
# files" for 30 minutes straight. Only phc-local-app/mobile/ is needed to
# build this app.
#
# .easignore REPLACES .gitignore for EAS's own archiving once it exists (it
# does not merge with it), so mobile's own node_modules/.expo excludes are
# repeated here explicitly rather than assumed inherited.

*
!phc-local-app/mobile/
!phc-local-app/mobile/**

phc-local-app/mobile/node_modules/
phc-local-app/mobile/.expo/
phc-local-app/mobile/dist/
phc-local-app/mobile/web-build/
